{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world","id":1517221,"title":"How can Avatars affect the physical world?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-05T12:31:06-07:00","id":1517221,"title":"How can Avatars affect the physical world?","content":"Considering no Manifeat Avatar merit, can Avatars show themselves to other people? Can they interact with the physical world somehow? Is there any raw regarding those kinds of limits?<br /> <br /> I'm asking this because I'm thinking about having an Avatar that is a long dead hermetic mage and have him as a mentor (pater). Would the Order be ok with that? Would they be able to prove the avatar's identity?<br /> <br /> Also, it would be a backstory only, with no mentor backgroud dots (but obviously some in Avatar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T15:12:31-07:00","id":1517228,"title":"","content":"Avatars are wholly in the storyteller's purview. They can do anything and everything as long as it's in the service of the path to Ascension. The ones that can manifest can just become physical in addition to doing things. The trick is that while they may act like people you know or you think you know, they are not those people they are just playing that because it's what YOU need to see. Also, they're not NPC's that care for your wellbeing or what you want - they are here to make you question yourself and Ascend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T21:46:31-07:00","id":1517246,"title":"","content":"As written, you can take your Manifest Avatar as an Ally, and it will be able to interact with others; but you need both the Manifest Avatar Merit and the Allies Background for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T09:54:54-07:00","id":1517286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517228#post1517228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avatars are wholly in the storyteller's purview. They can do anything and everything as long as it's in the service of the path to Ascension. The ones that can manifest can just become physical in addition to doing things. The trick is that while they may act like people you know or you think you know, they are not those people they are just playing that because it's what YOU need to see. Also, they're not NPC's that care for your wellbeing or what you want - they are here to make you question yourself and Ascend.</div> </div> </div> </div>But can other people see them, if they want to present themselves? I know that if a ST want they can. I'd like to know if there's any raw about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T09:57:44-07:00","id":1517287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517246#post1517246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written, you can take your Manifest Avatar as an Ally, and it will be able to interact with others; but you need both the Manifest Avatar Merit and the Allies Background for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But what about avatars that are not manifested (no merit)? Only the mage can see him? They don't have any means of showing or speaking with other ppl or mages?<br /> <br /> And what you think about the avatar being a long dead hermetic and working as a pater?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T10:29:42-07:00","id":1517290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517287#post1517287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. But what about avatars that are not manifested (no merit)? Only the mage can see him? They don't have any means of showing or speaking with other ppl or mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, it can only be seen by the Mage, though you as ST are not limited to that if you don't want to be and the player is okay with it (it's part of his character, he should have a say). The bigger question is why would the Avatar want to be visible?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what you think about the avatar being a long dead hermetic and working as a pater? </div> </div> </div>I generally don't put restrictions on what the Avatar can be, so that works for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T10:44:00-07:00","id":1517293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517286#post1517286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But can other people see them, if they want to present themselves? I know that if a ST want they can. I'd like to know if there's any raw about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Avatars aren't really a RAW thing by their definition. If they can manifest they can interact with others, but do keep in mind that Avatars are not really going to be sane in the human way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T12:36:31-07:00","id":1517298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517290#post1517290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bigger question is why would the Avatar want to be visible?</div> </div> </div> </div> He probably wouldn't want to be visible all the time. He would want that (maybe need?) to interact with other membera of the Order, idk.<br /> Do you think it could be a pater and teach the mage without ever being in contact with anyone else inside the Order? Would that be accepted?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517293#post1517293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Avatars aren't really a RAW thing by their definition. If they can manifest they can interact with others, but do keep in mind that Avatars are not really going to be sane in the human way.</div> </div> </div> </div>By manifest, you mean the merit, right?<br /> <br /> Also, idk why you say that they would be insane or not care for wellbeing of thr mage etc. I believe this van vary with each avatar and their relationahip with their mage. One thing is true for all, though, avatars wants to guide you magically.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T16:41:56-07:00","id":1517317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517287#post1517287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. But what about avatars that are not manifested (no merit)? Only the mage can see him? They don't have any means of showing or speaking with other ppl or mages?<br /> <br /> And what you think about the avatar being a long dead hermetic and working as a pater?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to RAW, if you don't have Manifest Avatar, you can't take your Avatar as an Ally. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAnd if you don't take your Avatar as an Ally, it isn't a separate character; at most, it's an \u201cimaginary friend\u201d like <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvey_(1950_film)\" target=\"_blank\">Harvey</a>. Without Manifest Avatar, its interaction with the mage is a lot more sporadic. With Circumspect Avatar, the Avatar never interacts with the mage in an \u201cimaginary friend\u201d sort of way. <br /> <br /> Finally: by default, a Manifest Avatar as an Ally <i>cannot be permanently killed</i>: if the Ally dies, it returns after an interval. But if you also take the Phylactery Flaw, your Manifest Avatar Ally <i>can</i> be killed \u2014 at which point you lose your Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T19:28:06-07:00","id":1517325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517317#post1517317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to RAW, if you don't have Manifest Avatar, you can't take your Avatar as an Ally. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAnd if you don't take your Avatar as an Ally, it isn't a separate character; at most, it's an \u201cimaginary friend\u201d like <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvey_(1950_film)\" target=\"_blank\">Harvey</a>. Without Manifest Avatar, its interaction with the mage is a lot more sporadic. With Circumspect Avatar, the Avatar never interacts with the mage in an \u201cimaginary friend\u201d sort of way.<br /> <br /> Finally: by default, a Manifest Avatar as an Ally <i>cannot be permanently killed</i>: if the Ally dies, it returns after an interval. But if you also take the Phylactery Flaw, your Manifest Avatar Ally <i>can</i> be killed \u2014 at which point you lose your Magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't expect the avatar to be an ally. Nor a separate character (with a sheet). But avatars seems (not definitely) to be outside entities.<br /> Also, I don't mind sporadic interactions, since all that is just part of backstory. The mage is no longer an apprentice and doesn't have a pater anymore. So the avatar can work normally. I just want to know if it is possible to have it as a pater. And how would that work inside the Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T02:03:43-07:00","id":1517338,"title":"","content":"Again. Just because the avatar claims it'a someone doesn't mean they are that person. This is something that the OoH would be well aware of.<br /> <br /> Avatars are often historical, mythological or personal history people - they become what they need to be for their Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T07:15:39-07:00","id":1517352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517338#post1517338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again. Just because the avatar claims it'a someone doesn't mean they are that person. This is something that the OoH would be well aware of.<br /> <br /> Avatars are often historical, mythological or personal history people - they become what they need to be for their Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. However, the veracity of the claim could be confirmed with magick, right? Maybe some Spirit and /or Prime to read some kind of identity or signature and confirm that the avatar is indeed an old hermetic.<br /> <br /> I mean, is it poaaible for an Avatar to *be* a long dead mage? Can a mage spirit really turn into an Avatar? If not, then it could be an avatar that belonged to said long dead mage...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T08:36:12-07:00","id":1517358,"title":"","content":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bUltimately, the only thing certain about the Avatar is that it's what gives the mage his Magick. As I showed before, it doesn't even have to be part of the mage, nor does it have to have a will of its own; though admittedly, both of those options are exceptions rather than the rule where traditional mages are concerned. And with those kinds of exceptions being possible, the idea that your Avatar is a long-dead mage is very much possible.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind that it's more <i>likely</i> that your mage simply inherited their Avatar from a long-dead mage; but if you want to say that the previous mage joined with their Avatar when they died, and that the Avatar now <i>is</i> the previous mage, then go for it!<br /> <br /> System-wise, you might consider taking the Mentor Background to represent your Avatar \u2014 although like the Ally Background, this combined with Manifest Avatar would essentially make your Avatar a separate character. Still, that separate character need not be physical; and while it might be <i>capable</i> of interacting with others besides you, it doesn't <i>have to be</i>. Or it could simply choose not to.<br /> <br /> Regardless, this would make the Avatar more significant than a mysterious figure that shows up primarily during Seekings, and would warrant the Manifest Avatar Merit. On the other hand, if you're fine with your Avatar mainly showing up in Seekings and only occasionally showing up otherwise, then you need neither Manifest Avatar nor Mentor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-08-2023, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T04:23:03-07:00","id":1517471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517352#post1517352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is true. However, the veracity of the claim could be confirmed with magick, right? Maybe some Spirit and /or Prime to read some kind of identity or signature and confirm that the avatar is indeed an old hermetic.<br /> <br /> I mean, is it poaaible for an Avatar to *be* a long dead mage? Can a mage spirit really turn into an Avatar? If not, then it could be an avatar that belonged to said long dead mage...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe so. Avatars are not people, nor are they ghosts of people. They are pieces of you that adapt how they act and how they are represented to you by what makes you tick. Any avatar claiming to be an actual person is not that person. What your character believes is a whole other kettle of fish, but avatars are narrative constructs meant to facilitate your Ascension and they are strange and hard to quantify. Not even the Masters of Prime and Spirit understand what avatars are, where they came from or how to make them do what they don't want to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T06:12:20-07:00","id":1517480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517471#post1517471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't believe so. Avatars are not people, nor are they ghosts of people. They are pieces of you that adapt how they act and how they are represented to you by what makes you tick. Any avatar claiming to be an actual person is not that person. What your character believes is a whole other kettle of fish, but avatars are narrative constructs meant to facilitate your Ascension and they are strange and hard to quantify. Not even the Masters of Prime and Spirit understand what avatars are, where they came from or how to make them do what they don't want to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally true. But <b>Mage</b> is full of odd corner cases, and Lord Revan's character could easily be one such case. Again, the only thing that's <i>absolutely</i> true about the Avatar is that it's what allows the mage to use Magick; <i>everything else</i> about it has exceptions. And in particular, the write-up for Manifest Avatar outright says that with that Merit, the Avatar <i>is</i> a person in and of itself, not merely a piece of the mage. <br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"> For most mages, the Avatar remains a mysterious figure, goading them from the sidelines and appearing primarily within a Seeking or during other moments of intense stress. For you, however, the Avatar is a vibrant presence in your life, as real to you as anyone else. <u>Essentially a character in its own right,</u> this manifested Avatar interacts with you on almost a daily basis. In certain situations, it might interact in other people, as manifestly real as any other person in your world.<br /> <br /> <u>The Manifest Avatar Merit embodies the Avatar as a full character under the Storyteller's control.</u> On its own, this Merit reflects that Avatar as a person who only the associated mage can see, hear, and interact with on a physical level; in conjunction with the Background: <b><i>Allies</i></b>, however, the Avatar becomes a character that <i>everyone</i> can see, hear, and feel.</span><br /> <b>Book of Secrets</b> p.71</div><br /> Remember that one thing about <b>Mage</b> is that it strives as much as possible to avoid saying that \u201cX is false; but your mage believes it anyway\u201d; even in the case of Quiet (which, to be clear, is <i>not</i> what I'm arguing this \u201cAvatar is a character\u201d stuff is), the things the mage believes are true if only in the sense of being hobgoblins or a Mindscape that the mage interacts with. If there's a way for something to be true <i>in your case</i>, even if not in general, then <b>Mage</b> tends to go for that over \u201cyou believe it, but you're wrong\u201d. And that's why the Manifest Avatar Merit is a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T06:24:54-07:00","id":1517483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517358#post1517358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that it's more <i>likely</i> that your mage simply inherited their Avatar from a long-dead mage; but if you want to say that the previous mage joined with their Avatar when they died, and that the Avatar now <i>is</i> the previous mage, them to for it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm.. Both would work, to be honest. I know that we don't have raw about how avatars are made. And that's intentional, to leave more room for creativity. But we know that when a mage dies, the avatar do not (necessarily), so it could be the avatar of a powerful long dead mage. But how and why could it be the merge of both avatar and mage?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517358#post1517358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">System-wise, you might consider taking the Mentor Background to represent your Avatar \u2014 although like the Ally Background, this combined with Manifest Avatar would essentially make your Avatar a separate character. Still, that separate character need not be physical; and while it might be <i>capable</i> of interacting with others besides you, it doesn't <i>have to be</i>. Or it could simply choose not to.<br /> <br /> Regardless, this would make the Avatar more significant than a mysterious figure that shows up primarily during Seekings, and would warrant the Manifest Avatar Merit. On the other hand, if you're fine with your Avatar mainly showing up in Seekings and only occasionally showing up otherwise, then you need neither Manifest Avatar nor Mentor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't want the avatar always around, so no mentor, ally or manifested. It is more part of the backstory of the mage. Of course, it will still show when doing seekings or in the moments he sees fit.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517471#post1517471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't believe so. Avatars are not people, nor are they ghosts of people. They are pieces of you that adapt how they act and how they are represented to you by what makes you tick. Any avatar claiming to be an actual person is not that person. What your character believes is a whole other kettle of fish, but avatars are narrative constructs meant to facilitate your Ascension and they are strange and hard to quantify. Not even the Masters of Prime and Spirit understand what avatars are, where they came from or how to make them do what they don't want to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any quote from the books to base that claim?<br /> <br /> <br /> And I made a little search and found this on M20:<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/NNkpFzy/avatar.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.ibb.co/NNkpFzy/avatar.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.ibb.co/NNkpFzy/avatar.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> So, it seems that avatars indeed can affect the real world and be seen by other people when they want. It also talks about they not violating Consensus, but I don't know if this means that they can do magick or if they are talking only about it appearence.<br /> <br /> About the Order interaction with it, there is a table that has &quot;See Avatar&quot; as Mind 3/Prime 2 /Spirit 1 in M20 page 509. So, the mages of the Order can use magick to see it and probably to confirm his identity as the avatar of the dead mage (or that it is the dead mage if I go this way) through Resonance or something like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T06:35:38-07:00","id":1517485,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't put too much weight on the frequency of appearance mentioned under Manifest Avatar; the important thing is that that Merit makes it a separate character under the Storyteller's control. I would say that the distinction between \u201cAvatar of a dead mage\u201d vs. \u201cthe dead mage itself\u201d would be whether or not you have this Merit: if the former, you probably don't need Manifest Avatar; of the latter, you need it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T07:50:01-07:00","id":1517489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517483#post1517483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have any quote from the books to base that claim?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No. Because the game intentionally leaves the avatars as nebulous, unquantifiable and ununderstandable. So you're not going to find roleplaying notes or explanations of what they are and where they came from. RAW is irrelevant to Avatars because they are a narrative tool for the Storyteller to facilitate the quest to Ascension.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T11:25:37-07:00","id":1517506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517485#post1517485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't put too much weight on the frequency of appearance mentioned under Manifest Avatar; the important thing is that that Merit makes it a separate character under the Storyteller's control. I would say that the distinction between \u201cAvatar of a dead mage\u201d vs. \u201cthe dead mage itself\u201d would be whether or not you have this Merit: if the former, you probably don't need Manifest Avatar; of the latter, you need it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about that. I think that, whilr the player chooses what his avatar looks like, his personality and etc., the ST decides when to show him and controls him in game. The player just creates the backstory. So, all avatars are under ST control, being manifested or not.<br /> <br /> The merit specifies that, while normal avatars only show in seekings or special ocasions (when he wants), the ones with the merit are much nore present. If you buy ally too, then it can be a real physical being.<br /> <br /> So, I believe that the fact that the avatar *is* a long dead mage or just the mage's avatar isn't related to the merit or background.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I don't want a physical avatar, nor a more present one. So, not manifested nor ally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517489#post1517489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Because the game intentionally leaves the avatars as nebulous, unquantifiable and ununderstandable. So you're not going to find roleplaying notes or explanations of what they are and where they came from. RAW is irrelevanr\u00e7t to Avatars because they are a narrative tool for the Storyteller to facilitate the quest to Ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see. Then there is a possibility of the avatar being a long dead mage. But wither way would be cool, maybe it might make more sense if it was just the mage's avatar. I don't remember if raw says what happns exactly when a mage die...<br /> <br /> Anyway, it is clear now that the avatar can show himself to others if he wants and mages can also see them with magick, so the avatar could work as a pater. (I still don't now if the avatar can use magick, though).<br /> <br /> Now, it is known that avatars can be evil. How could that affect the mage? How much influence would it have on their host? It wouldn't necessarily be bad torwards the mage nor harm him, but definitely have evil ideas and advices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T13:37:51-07:00","id":1517516,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517485#post1517485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't put too much weight on the frequency of appearance mentioned under Manifest Avatar; the important thing is that that Merit makes it a separate character under the Storyteller's control. I would say that the distinction between \u201cAvatar of a dead mage\u201d vs. \u201cthe dead mage itself\u201d would be whether or not you have this Merit: if the former, you probably don't need Manifest Avatar; of the latter, you need it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about that. I think that, whilr the player chooses what his avatar looks like, his personality and etc., the ST decides when to show him and controls him in game. The player just creates the backstory. So, all avatars are under ST control, being manifested or not.<br /> <br /> The merit specifies that, while normal avatars only show in seekings or special ocasions (when he wants), the ones with the merit are much nore present. If you buy ally too, then it can be a real physical being.<br /> <br /> So, I believe that the fact that the avatar *is* a long dead mage or just the mage's avatar isn't related to the merit or background.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I don't want a physical avatar, nor a more present one. So, not manifested nor ally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1517489#post1517489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Because the game intentionally leaves the avatars as nebulous, unquantifiable and ununderstandable. So you're not going to find roleplaying notes or explanations of what they are and where they came from. RAW is irrelevanr\u00e7t to Avatars because they are a narrative tool for the Storyteller to facilitate the quest to Ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see. Then there is a possibility of the avatar being a long dead mage. But wither way would be cool, maybe it might make more sense if it was just the mage's avatar. I don't remember if raw says what happns exactly when a mage die...<br /> <br /> Anyway, it is clear now that the avatar can show himself to others if he wants and mages can also see them with magick, so the avatar could work as a pater. (I still don't now if the avatar can use magick, though).<br /> <br /> Now, it is known that avatars can be evil. How could that affect the mage? How much influence would it have on their host? It wouldn't necessarily be bad torwards the mage nor harm him, but definitely have evil ideas and advices.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T16:50:30-07:00","id":1517523,"title":"","content":"You're in Storyteller country. You either decide if you're one or ask yours to call it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T05:48:08-07:00","id":1518753,"title":"","content":"Because this is Mage, I think it's fair to ask: what do you imagine the difference to be between an Avatar that presents as a long-dead Hermetic and one who &quot;is&quot; a long-dead Hermetic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T18:52:03-07:00","id":1518801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1518753#post1518753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because this is Mage, I think it's fair to ask: what do you imagine the difference to be between an Avatar that presents as a long-dead Hermetic and one who &quot;is&quot; a long-dead Hermetic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I believe that if the avatar &quot;was&quot; the long dead mage, he would have been through all what that mage has gone, having all the knowledge and experience he had. While an avatar presenting as the dead mage would be just some impersonator. <br /> <br /> What is the difference between an actor that plays Nikola Tesla and the actual Nikola Tesla?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T19:29:16-07:00","id":1518866,"title":"","content":"The avatar can be whatever it needs to be, and so there's no reason it couldn't do an <i>arbitrarily good </i>impersonation.<br /> <br /> I think it's not so much actor vs actual; it's more like &quot;if you could make a perfect replica of yourself, how would you tell which one was the original? Is the question even a meaningful one?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T16:40:27-07:00","id":1518969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1518866#post1518866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The avatar can be whatever it needs to be, and so there's no reason it couldn't do an <i>arbitrarily good </i>impersonation.<br /> <br /> I think it's not so much actor vs actual; it's more like &quot;if you could make a perfect replica of yourself, how would you tell which one was the original? Is the question even a meaningful one?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure an avatar could be a replica with on the level of having the exact same knowledge, personality, experience, etc.<br /> if they can, then the question kinda lost its meaning, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T05:07:08-07:00","id":1519102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1518969#post1518969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure an avatar could be a replica with on the level of having the exact same knowledge, personality, experience, etc.<br /> if they can, then the question kinda lost its meaning, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Avatar is what you think the mentor was and nothing beyond that. It's unconcerned with the world beyond what it needs to get you moving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T02:45:21-07:00","id":1519721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1517221-how-can-avatars-affect-the-physical-world?p=1518801#post1518801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the difference between an actor that plays Nikola Tesla and the actual Nikola Tesla?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the actual and real Nicola Tesla a Tradition Mage from the Society of the Ether ?<br /> With some definite achievments, fame, and knowledge, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user